  "id": "COMPOUND:17465 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "Sodium 4-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzoate is implicated in the biological activity against FaDu through multiple pathways, all of which converge on the target FaDu. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for several metabolites, including (+)-(8S,8'R)-9-acetoxy-4,4'-dihydroxy-3,3',5'-trimethoxylignan, Phlorigidoside C, and Sophoradiol. These metabolites are all known to interact with FaDu, indicating a shared mechanism of action that involves the target cell. The presence of multiple distinct targets, all leading to the same final outcome, supports a potential role for Sodium 4-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzoate in modulating FaDu activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism involving the regulation of FaDu through the interaction of various metabolites, which may be relevant in the context of drug development and therapeutic applications.",
